<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- MapSettingsTab — the Map tab of the Settings window: the app's THEME, the BASEMAP under it, and
     the library of imported basemap styles.

       ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
       │  ⌄  Theme                                            │
       │    [Anvil Dark              ]                        │  <- the IDENTITY: app chrome +
       │    Sets the app's chrome, the map page's…               the page's colours + the
       ├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤     basemap, all together
       │  ⌄  Basemap                                          │
       │    [Data Viz Black          ]                        │  <- STYLE (an OVERRIDE of the
       │                                                      │     theme's, for this session)
       │    ────────────────────────────────────              │
       │    C:\Users\...\Desktop           [Browse…]          │  <- the SOURCE pair: offline
       │    Found usa_full.pmtiles.                           │     is a FOLDER, online is a
       │    [ ] Use online tiles                              │     URL. Both stay editable
       │    [https://api.protomaps…]                          │     whichever is active - you
       │    Offline — bundled PMTiles.                        │     set one up BEFORE switching
       ├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
       │  ⌄  Styles                                           │
       │    [Import style…]                                   │  <- author in MAPUTNIK, import the
       │    Imported "Night Ops" and selected it.             │     result. There is no in-app
       │    Night Ops                             [Remove]    │     editor - see the note below
       └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

     WHAT BELONGS IN THIS TAB: the app's LOOK — the theme, and the basemap it draws itself over, plus
     where that basemap's tiles come from.
     ⚠️ THE THEME IS APP-WIDE, NOT MAP-ONLY — it sets the window chrome too — and it is here rather than in
     a tab of its own because it OWNS the basemap below it, and separating a thing from the thing it
     controls is how the two drift. Revisit if the theme ever grows options that have nothing to do with
     the map. What the map DRAWS on top (the radar-site marker networks) is the Radar tab
     next door. The older, wider rule still holds underneath both: nothing in
     either tab repeats per pane — a control needing a copy per pane belongs in RadarControls.

     ⚠️ IT USED TO OWN THE CAMERA TOO, and no longer does. Fit to view and Reset north went to
     Composites/MapControlsStrip; the CONUS checkbox, the "isolate a state (hover & click)" checkbox and
     the state-name combo went with them, collapsed into that strip's ONE isolation combo (No Isolation /
     Isolate CONUS / Select to Isolate / the 52 states). All of it is a GESTURE you make while reading the
     map, which is the same test that pulled Markers and Inspect out of the Radar tab; what is left here is
     a PREFERENCE you set once.
     ⚠️ Do NOT re-add the camera controls to fill this tab out. One control in two places is one that
     will drift.

     ⚠️ THE OFFLINE FOLDER ROW IS THE OLD SettingsDialog, INLINED - AND THAT DIALOG IS NOW DELETED. It did
     exactly this job and NOTHING opened it (its caller was lost in a UI rewrite), which left "name the file
     usa_full.pmtiles and drop it on your Desktop" as the only way to load a basemap, with a missing file
     rendering as a black map and no error at all. It belongs HERE because the folder IS the offline tile
     source, so it sits beside the online URL rather than in Storage. The dialog was deleted rather than
     kept alongside: one control in two places is one that will drift.
     ⚠️ A FOLDER CHANGE NEEDS A RESTART, and the status line says so once you change one. The mapdata host
     is mapped once, in MainWindow's WebView bootstrap, before any page loads - so unlike the online URL
     below it, this cannot be applied live. Don't add an "apply now" button; it would have to re-run the
     whole bootstrap.

     This was the top half of the former MapControlsWindow, which is now two tabs rather than one long
     scroll. -->

<UserControl x:Class="Anvil.Controls.Composites.MapSettingsTab"
             xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             xmlns:d="http://schemas.microsoft.com/expression/blend/2008"
             xmlns:mc="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006"
             mc:Ignorable="d">

    <!-- Body: one Expander per section (Styles.xaml SectionExpanderStyle), grid rows inside each. -->
    <Grid RowSpacing="8" VerticalAlignment="Top">
        <Grid.RowDefinitions>
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- theme -->
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- basemap -->
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- styles: import library -->
        </Grid.RowDefinitions>

        <!-- THEME. Above Basemap because it OWNS the basemap: picking a theme sets the style below it.
             ⚠️ The two are knowingly redundant right now. Two themes cover two of the five bundled styles,
             so the Basemap combo stays as an override for the other three — see the note on it. When the
             theme list either grows to cover every style or the extra styles are dropped, that combo goes
             and this one is the only picker. Don't "tidy" the pair by deleting this one. -->
        <Expander Grid.Row="0" Header="Theme" IsExpanded="True"
                  Style="{StaticResource SectionExpanderStyle}">
            <Grid RowSpacing="4">
                <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- Theme combo -->
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- what it covers -->
                </Grid.RowDefinitions>

                <ComboBox Grid.Row="0" Margin="4,0,0,0"
                          Width="240" HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                          ItemsSource="{x:Bind ViewModel.AvailableThemes}"
                          DisplayMemberPath="DisplayName"
                          SelectedItem="{x:Bind ViewModel.SelectedTheme, Mode=TwoWay}"
                          ToolTipService.ToolTip="The app's visual identity: window chrome and the basemap under it"/>

                <TextBlock Grid.Row="1" Margin="4,2,0,0" TextWrapping="Wrap" MaxWidth="360"
                           HorizontalAlignment="Left" Opacity="0.75"
                           Text="Sets the app's chrome, the map page's colours and the basemap. Applies immediately."/>
            </Grid>
        </Expander>

        <Expander Grid.Row="1" Header="Basemap" IsExpanded="True"
                  Style="{StaticResource SectionExpanderStyle}">
            <Grid RowSpacing="8">
                <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- Basemap combo -->
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- rule -->
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- Offline source: folder + Browse -->
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- Offline source: status / restart note -->
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- Use online tiles -->
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- Online tiles URL -->
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- Tile source status -->
                </Grid.RowDefinitions>

                <!-- ⚠️ AN OVERRIDE OF THE THEME'S BASEMAP, AND IT PERSISTS. The theme above owns a basemap
                     and sets this when it changes; picking one here diverges from the theme until you
                     change theme again. ⚠️ It used to be session-only, deliberately — importing a style
                     reversed that, because a theme names a BUNDLED style and an import would therefore be
                     deselected on every launch. Empty in settings means "follow the theme".
                     ⚠️ ItemsSource is an ObservableCollection so an IMPORT appears here immediately;
                     ViewModel.RefreshStyles() is what re-reads it. -->
                <ComboBox Grid.Row="0" Margin="4,0,0,0"
                          Width="240" HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                          ItemsSource="{x:Bind ViewModel.AvailableStyles}"
                          DisplayMemberPath="DisplayName"
                          SelectedItem="{x:Bind ViewModel.SelectedStyle, Mode=TwoWay}"
                          ToolTipService.ToolTip="The basemap drawn under everything"/>

                <Border Grid.Row="1" Height="1" Margin="4,10,0,4" HorizontalAlignment="Left" Width="360"
                        Background="{ThemeResource CardStrokeColorDefaultSolidBrush}"/>

                <!-- OFFLINE SOURCE: the folder holding the ~29 GB usa_full.pmtiles archive.
                     ⚠️ The path is READ-ONLY text, not a TextBox. A hand-typed path that does not exist fails
                     silently at the NEXT launch as a black map - the exact failure this row exists to end -
                     and the folder picker cannot produce one. -->
                <Grid Grid.Row="2" Margin="4,0,0,0" ColumnSpacing="8" HorizontalAlignment="Left" Width="360">
                    <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                    </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                    <TextBlock Grid.Column="0" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                               TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis"
                               Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.MapDataFolder, Mode=OneWay}"
                               ToolTipService.ToolTip="{x:Bind ViewModel.MapDataFolder, Mode=OneWay}"/>
                    <Button Grid.Column="1" Content="Browse…" Click="OnBrowseMapDataClick"
                            ToolTipService.ToolTip="Pick the folder holding the offline basemap archive"/>
                </Grid>

                <!-- Whether the archive is actually THERE, plus - once changed - that it takes a restart.
                     ⚠️ One line, not two: both answer the same question ("will the map draw?"), and a separate
                     restart row would sit empty for the whole life of a normal session. -->
                <TextBlock Grid.Row="3" Margin="4,4,0,0"
                           TextWrapping="Wrap" MaxWidth="360" HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                           Text="{x:Bind MapDataLine(ViewModel.MapDataStatus, ViewModel.MapDataFolderChanged), Mode=OneWay}"
                           Style="{StaticResource SettingsFieldLabelStyle}"/>

                <!-- Tile SOURCE — orthogonal to the style above. The styles are Protomaps-schema styles, so every
                     one of them renders identically against either source; this only changes where the vector
                     tiles come from. Offline is the default and the fallback. -->
                <CheckBox Grid.Row="4" Margin="4,4,0,0"
                          Content="Use online tiles (needs a network connection)"
                          IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.UseOnlineTiles, Mode=TwoWay}"
                          ToolTipService.ToolTip="Stream the basemap instead of reading the bundled offline PMTiles file. The map's look is unchanged — same styles, same fonts."/>

                <!-- TwoWay on LostFocus (the x:Bind default), deliberately NOT PropertyChanged: pushing a
                     half-typed URL would re-style every pane on each keystroke.
                     ⚠️ Stays ENABLED while offline on purpose — you paste the key BEFORE flipping the toggle, and
                     disabling it would force the trip through an unusable online state to configure one. -->
                <TextBox Grid.Row="5" Margin="4,2,0,0"
                         Width="360" HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                         PlaceholderText="https://api.protomaps.com/tiles/v4.json?key=…"
                         Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.OnlineTilesUrl, Mode=TwoWay}"
                         ToolTipService.ToolTip="A Protomaps-schema source: the Protomaps API TileJSON (free for non-commercial use, needs your key), a {z}/{x}/{y} template, or a self-hosted pmtiles:// archive."/>

                <TextBlock Grid.Row="6" Margin="4,2,0,0"
                           TextWrapping="Wrap" MaxWidth="360" HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                           Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.TileSourceStatus, Mode=OneWay}"
                           Style="{StaticResource SettingsFieldLabelStyle}"/>
            </Grid>
        </Expander>


        <!-- STYLES: importing and removing style documents.
             ⚠️ IMPORT IS THE WHOLE STORY — THERE IS NO IN-APP EDITOR, BY DECISION. A live colour tuner
             (a global levels grade + a per-slot override table + a positional export that rewrote the
             style file's Nth #rrggbb literal) was built and then REMOVED: re-colouring a basemap is a
             job Maputnik already does properly, and matching it would have meant growing widths,
             opacities, fonts, filters and zoom stops — a style editor, in a weather app. So the app owns
             one half of that loop and owns it well: you author elsewhere, import the result here, and it
             becomes a real selectable basemap. ⚠️ Don't re-add an editor; extend the IMPORT if something
             is missing.
             ⚠️ It sits BELOW Basemap because an import SELECTS itself in that picker — the two rows are
             one gesture read downward. -->
        <Expander Grid.Row="2" Header="Styles" IsExpanded="True"
                  Style="{StaticResource SectionExpanderStyle}">
            <Grid RowSpacing="10">
                <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- import button -->
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- status / error line -->
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- imported list -->
                </Grid.RowDefinitions>

                <StackPanel Grid.Row="0" Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="8" Margin="4,0,0,0">
                    <Button Content="Import style…" Click="OnImportStyleClick"
                            ToolTipService.ToolTip="Add a MapLibre style document to your library"/>
                </StackPanel>

                <!-- ⚠️ THE ERROR CHANNEL. An import can fail for reasons the user can act on (not JSON, no
                     layers, no sources), and a picker that silently does nothing is the worst version of
                     that. Same footer-carries-the-failure shape the temporal cards use. -->
                <TextBlock Grid.Row="1" Margin="4,0,0,0" TextWrapping="Wrap" MaxWidth="360"
                           FontSize="12"
                           Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}"
                           Text="{x:Bind ImportStatus, Mode=OneWay}"/>

                <!-- Imported styles only: the bundled five are not removable, so listing them here would
                     be a list where most rows do nothing. -->
                <!-- ⚠️ ItemsSource is assigned in CODE, not x:Bind. MapStyle is a RECORD, and x:Bind on a
                     collection of one makes the XAML type-info generator emit setters for its init-only
                     properties, which does not compile (CS8852). Nothing here needs the compiled binding:
                     the rows are two fields and a button. -->
                <ItemsControl x:Name="ImportedList" Grid.Row="2" Margin="4,0,0,0" MaxWidth="360"
                              HorizontalAlignment="Left">
                    <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                        <!-- ⚠️ {Binding}, NOT x:Bind. MapStyle is a RECORD, so its properties are init-only,
                             and an x:DataType makes the XAML type-info generator emit setters for them —
                             which does not compile (CS8852). {Binding} generates no type info at all.
                             The same reason ForeCastTab binds its legend rows this way. -->
                        <DataTemplate>
                            <Grid ColumnSpacing="8" Padding="0,3">
                                <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                                    <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                                    <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                                </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                                <TextBlock Grid.Column="0" Text="{Binding DisplayName}" FontSize="12"
                                           VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                           TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis"/>
                                <Button Grid.Column="1" Content="Remove" FontSize="12"
                                        Tag="{Binding FileName}"
                                        Click="OnRemoveStyleClick"/>
                            </Grid>
                        </DataTemplate>
                    </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                </ItemsControl>
            </Grid>
        </Expander>

    </Grid>
</UserControl>
